Sumayah aka the winner of the half-court shot challenge at the camp. 

@sumayah.sugapong is a standout 5’7” guard known for her scoring ability, playmaking feel, and strong defensive presence. At UC San Diego, she became one of the conference’s top performers, earning First Team All Big West, Big West Tournament MVP, and helping lead UCSD to its first ever NCAA Division I Tournament appearance.

In 2025, she transferred to the University of Arizona, bringing her shot creation, competitiveness, and big game composure to the Wildcats. Sugapong also represents the Philippines women’s national team, solidifying herself as one of the most exciting young guards in the region.

7️⃣th place at my World Triathlon Cup debut in Florianópolis 🇧🇷!!!

Somebody pinch me! Being back on the blue carpet after 1.5 years felt very special — excited, grateful, emotional… 💙

So beyond grateful for everyone who kept believing in me and stuck with me through this “not always easy or pleasant” journey. Your love and support kept me going every single day 🫶🏼

Finishing this season with my World Triathlon Cup debut was really special but crossing the finish line in 7th took it to another level! 💃✨

Lessons learned and SO excited for what’s next!

Obrigada Floripa 🥹🇧🇷✨

